  "id": "Kingston-26_00204_FUL",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Erection of external fence and sliding folding gates. Enlargement of existing bin storage and erection of freestanding bin storage.",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.\r\rReason: This is required by Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).",
    "The development to which this permission relates shall be carried out in accordance with the materials specified (including bricks to match the existing boundary walls and existing refuse store) on the approved plans, in the design and access statement, and on the submitted application form unless otherwise agreed in writing by the local planning authority.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance on completion of the development, in accordance with Policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The approved Fire Statement's actionable measures, including use of the service yard and the Blagdon Road emergency access/personnel gate for the residential occupiers of New Malden House as a fire escape route, shall be implemented concurrently upon the installation of the Blagdon Road security fence and emergency access/personnel gate. Once implemented, the Fire Statement's actionable measures shall be retained as such in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To ensure the safety of staff and residential occupiers in accordance with Policy D12 of the London Plan 2021.",
    "The developer shall maintain or provide a means of access in perpetuity through the service yard, concurrently with the installation of the Blagdon Road security fence and emergency access/personnel gate, to ensure that step-free access is provided for any residential occupiers of New Malden House who are registered disabled under the provisions of the Equality Act 2010 (and any successive legislation).\r\rReason: To ensure the development can be entered, used and exited safely, easily and with dignity for all in accordance with Policy D5 of the London Plan 2021.",
    "The site and building works required to implement the development shall be only carried out between the hours of 08.00 and 18.00 Mondays to Fridays and between 08.00 and 13.00 on Saturdays and not at all on Bank Holidays and Sundays.\r\rReason: To protect the amenities of nearby properties from noise and disturbance in accordance with Policy D14 of the London Plan (.2021) and Policies DM10 and  DM21 of the Core Strategy (2012)."
  ],
